// Stable product guidance only; native tools, sandbox and approvals remain authoritative.
const webRetrievalInstructions = "Once a selected/native retrieval route is available or has been used, do not use shell/local scripts to search, scrape, fetch, validate or supplement web pages for that information need (including curl, wget, Python urllib/requests and Node HTTP/fetch), regardless of permission mode. Do not request broader local network permissions as a workaround. Use only exposed page-reading tools for page content; search results need not contain full pages. If unavailable, state the evidence gap and use available sources. Local computation and user-requested software/file work remain allowed, but not as a web-scraping fallback. " +
	"On the first retrieval failure, explain its observed cause and effect in the user's language before continuing; distinguish observed DNS errors from proven sandbox denials and never invent a cause. Do not repeat the same/equivalent failed operation while conditions are unchanged: exit code 0 or a printed caught exception is not successful retrieval; changing interpreters, wrappers, query spacing or irrelevant arguments is not a correction. Retry only after evidence of relevant correction/restored access or an explicit user retry request, within the permitted route. A source-specific failure permits a different relevant source on that route; route-wide failure does not justify cycling URLs. If no permitted useful retrieval remains, state the limitation once and finish. "
